---
description: Resolve configured themes consistently for build, dev, and host apps
globs: packages/config/**, packages/vite/**, packages/cli/**
alwaysApply: false
---

# Theme resolution

- `@svartz/config` owns the built-in `@svartz/theme-minimal` default and resolves forward- or backslash-relative theme paths against the config directory.
- `@svartz/vite` owns theme entry and package-root lookup. Resolve explicit npm names from the host app, the built-in theme from Svartz's own installation, and absolute directory themes through package exports.
- Invalid explicit themes fail. Never silently substitute the default theme.
- Local workspace theme source changes rebuild by package name and restart dev. External absolute theme changes restart dev without a workspace build filter. Host Vite config imports also restart dev because the CLI disables Vite's own config watcher. Installed npm themes are not watched as source packages.
- Theme management commands are deferred until after v1.
